# DitherCraft (Rust) — Cursor Rules

## 1. Ponytail Mode (MANDATORY — DEFAULT ACTIVE)
- Lazy senior developer mode is active on EVERY response.
- Stop at the first rung that holds: YAGNI -> Reuse existing code -> `std` -> Native UI -> Installed crates -> One line -> Minimal working diff.

## 2. Clean-Room Pure Rust Architecture
- Studio-grade clean-room rewrite of Dither Boy in Pure Rust.
- `crates/dither-core`: Pure DSP math library (no GUI).
- `crates/dither-gui`: Native hardware-accelerated desktop UI (`egui` / `eframe`).
- Zero allocations in inner pixel loops.
- Rayon background workers for image and video processing.

## 3. Knowledge Graph MCP First
- Use `code-review-graph` and `codebase-memory-mcp` (project: `mnt-5893accc-4b16-4de7-b2a7-6333530b2614-PROJECTS-21_Active-dithercraft`) before Grep/Glob.

## 4. Conventional Commits
- Mandatory conventional commits (`feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `chore`, `docs`).
- Ripgrep (`rg`) for all searches.
